# Project rules

Before coding, list the files you will create or change and wait for an OK.

Finish every task by running `./gradlew assembleDebug testDebugUnitTest` and fixing all errors.

Never use `fallbackToDestructiveMigration`. Every schema change gets a version bump, a `Migration`, and a migration test.

```kotlin
@Database(version = 2, exportSchema = true)
abstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase()

val MIGRATION_1_2 = object : Migration(1, 2) {
    override fun migrate(db: SupportSQLiteDatabase) {
        db.execSQL("ALTER TABLE session ADD COLUMN note TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''")
    }
}
```

The domain layer is pure Kotlin (no `android.*` imports). Time comes only from an injected `java.time.Clock`.

Every engine and use case gets unit tests.

ViewModels expose one `StateFlow<UiState>` plus `onEvent(Event)` (MVI).

```kotlin
val uiState: StateFlow<SessionUiState>
fun onEvent(event: SessionEvent)
```

Never hardcode exercise names. Everything is data-driven.

kg only. Network is allowed only in `WeatherRepository`, and failures are silent.

Workout screens: minimum 72dp touch targets, and no swipe-only or long-press-only critical actions.
